# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.
#
# Rules here are deliberately TARGETED rather than broad. An earlier version of this
# file ignored `scripts`, `docs/` and `.claude/` wholesale and then re-admitted a few
# paths from a block at the very end, which meant the meaning of a rule depended on
# its line number. It also silently swallowed real work: six working scripts, the
# matchmaking test harnesses among them, never showed up in `git status` at all.
# Keep new rules narrow, and keep any negation directly beneath the rule it undoes.

# ── Secrets. Never commit. ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Covers .env, .env.local, .env.production, .env.migration and friends at any depth.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.jks
*.mobileprovision
# Agent tooling writes credentials straight into these.
*.local.json
claude-flow.config.json

# ── Sensitive data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Imported class rosters: names + emails for ~6.6k real students who have no
# Proximity account. Bulk PII, never committed.
class_db/
# Database migration artifacts and dumps.
backups/
*.dump
backup_*.sql
backup_pre_v4_*
# Supabase CLI local state, may contain project refs / connection info.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# ── Dependencies (any depth, for the monorepo) ────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js
.yarn/install-state.gz

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
# Build dir for the local content-recording mode (`npm run dev:demo`).
.next-demo/
out/
build/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.vercel

# ── Expo / React Native (apps/mobile) ─────────────────────────────────────────
.expo/
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/ios/

# ── OS, editor and debug junk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.orig.*
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Local agent + tool state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .claude/skills/ IS committed so the team shares slash commands. Only per-machine
# state is ignored, named file by file so a new skill can never be swallowed.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude-flow/
.codex
.swarm
.swarm/memory.db
.agents
# The MCP knowledge base (mcp/knowledge/) is COMMITTED so every machine and coding
# agent shares the same repo knowledge. Regenerate with
# `node mcp/scripts/generate-knowledge.mjs` and commit alongside code changes;
# CI (update-knowledge.yml) opens a sync PR for any drift on staging/main.
# Only the local agent-swarm runtime log stays machine-local:
mcp/knowledge/agent-sessions.json
# .mcp.json is committed so the team shares MCP server setup. It contains no
# secrets: the Supabase access token is env-interpolated (${SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN}).

# ── Generated reports and research artifacts ──────────────────────────────────
# scripts/ itself is TRACKED. Only generated output under it is ignored.
scripts/matchmaking-reports/
scripts/seo-engine/reports/*.md
# CI impact-check artifacts.
ci-out/
# Firecrawl scrape output (research artifacts, not source).
.firecrawl/
# Local image dump, not served from git.
public/listing-pics

# ── Personal scratch notes (deliberate, not accidental) ───────────────────────
TODO.md
today.md
